Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: preserve the parent node reference during child lookup

of_find_node_by_name() consumes a reference to its starting node. Passing
dev->of_node without taking a reference drops the parent's reference
twice on each probe, causing refcount warnings and a crash on reload.

Only children of the Venus node are relevant here.
Use of_get_child_by_name() to preserve the parent's reference.

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -307,7 +307,7 @@ static int venus_add_video_core(struct venus_core *core, const char *node_name,
 	if (!node_name)
 		return 0;
 
-	enp = of_find_node_by_name(dev->of_node, node_name);
+	enp = of_get_child_by_name(dev->of_node, node_name);
 	if (enp) {
 		of_node_put(enp);
 		return 0;
